pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The cardinality boundary sits one unit FURTHER out than the general-PB one, because the
% decrement is per literal: with two literals mapped to TRUE, `i64::MIN + 1` still wraps (on the
% second decrement) and only `i64::MIN + 2` does not. This is that control, and it is refused by
% the unfixed checker too.
f 2;
rup 1 x1 1 x2 >= -9223372036854775806 ;
red 1 ~x1 >= 1 : x1 -> 1 ;
pol 1 4 +;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 5;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
